WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.106
Feedback is the connection between action and improvement.

2
00:00:03.106 --> 00:00:15.144
Without feedback, people may not know whether their decisions are getting better, whether they are solving the right problem, or whether they are only becoming more confident in a weak method.

3
00:00:15.144 --> 00:00:19.803
Timely feedback is easier to connect to the action that produced it.

4
00:00:19.803 --> 00:00:27.181
Specific feedback is easier to use because it points to what should be repeated, changed, or examined more closely.

5
00:00:27.181 --> 00:00:31.064
Expert coaching can accelerate development by making invisible judgment visible.

6
00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:39.995
A coach can explain what they noticed, which cue changed their interpretation, why they rejected an option, or how they checked for error.

7
00:00:39.995 --> 00:00:47.761
Peer review and self-review can also support expertise when they focus on evidence and reasoning instead of personal preference.

8
00:00:47.761 --> 00:00:53.197
Performance data, simulations, and scenario reviews give learners a clearer mirror than memory alone.

9
00:00:53.197 --> 00:00:58.245
Weak feedback environments are dangerous because they allow habits to form without correction.

10
00:00:58.245 --> 00:01:06.011
If errors are delayed, hidden, normalized, or never connected back to the original decision, people can develop confidence without improvement.

11
00:01:06.011 --> 00:01:12.223
In some workplaces, the same process may appear successful because downstream teams quietly fix the problems.

12
00:01:12.223 --> 00:01:17.271
That protects the outcome in the moment but prevents the performer from learning.

13
00:01:17.271 --> 00:01:20.766
Error correction is most useful before mistakes become automatic.

14
00:01:20.766 --> 00:01:23.872
A strong learning environment treats errors as information.

15
00:01:23.872 --> 00:01:33.192
It asks what the person saw, what they missed, what assumption shaped the action, and what cue should guide a better response next time.

16
00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.910
The point is not to punish imperfection.

17
00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:42.511
The point is to keep performance aligned with reality while the learner is still able to adjust.
